1. The application: PyGoat
--------------------------

Copyright (c) 2020 pygoat
https://github.com/adeyosemanputra/pygoat

A deliberately vulnerable Django application, vendored here unmodified as a test
fixture for the pipeline. Taken by way of
https://github.com/nanuchi/devsecops-crash-course-pygoat.

These paths are upstream's:

    pygoat/  chatbot/  Solutions/  introduction/
    manage.py  setup.py  PyGoatBot.py  installer.sh  uninstaller.py
    uninstaller.sh  gh-md-toc  Procfile  runtime.txt  requirements.txt
    docker-compose.yml  temp.py  test.log  .all-contributorsrc
    .vscode/settings.json  docs/dev_guide.md

Upstream's README is preserved in full at the end of this repository's README,
and its contributor list with it. Upstream's own CI workflow
(.github/workflows/main.yml) was replaced, not extended.

Because this application exists to be exploitable, it must not be deployed
anywhere reachable. deploy/ exists to be scanned and policy-tested.

